{"kind":"charness.bounded_review.v1","lens":"release lock-in final pass","verdict":"pass","target_observations":null,"findings":[],"counterweight_triage":[{"concern":"The release notes say a reader-probe start is unnamed, but omit the spec’s explicit caveat that it is also uncounted. In context, a reader could assume it appears in the count of unnamed commands.","bin":"advisory","disposition":"The exception is disclosed as unseen and unnamed, and the spec states the count behavior accurately. Consider adding “and is not counted” to the notes for consistency."},{"concern":"The agent-task-runs summary says a seen young command “delays either a check,” though the due check runs and defers its action.","bin":"advisory","disposition":"The linked spec gives the detailed behavior. Consider changing the summary to say the action is deferred at a due check."}],"next_move":"Lock in the follow-up; the followup33 timing finding is fixed. The docstring and spec distinguish a start first seen during the rule’s tree probe from a start still unseen by the event reader. The spec’s second-check timing and fourth-check reclamation summary agree with the bound test’s expected sequence. The reader-probe exception is accurately described in the spec: while the reader is held probing or writing, a start may remain unseen and be interrupted without being named or counted.","non_claims":["Reviewed the 20 identity-bound inline paths; did not inspect workspace paths or run tests/live probes.","The supplied goal lineage is not-goal-bound; this review does not close a Goal Run.","The 1.0-second test window rationale is recorded in the test comment; this review did not independently verify behavior under coverage."]}
